[node name="StoryItems" type="Node2D" parent="."]

[node name="SeamWall" type="Area2D" parent="StoryItems"]
z_index = 6
position = Vector2(0, -360)
collision_layer = 16
collision_mask = 1
script = ExtResource("3_story_item")
interaction_name = "Read the names on the seam"
flag_to_set = "pit_seam_names_seen"
discovery_text = "[b]Names in the seam[/b]

Where the white vein runs out of the rock, the wall is cut with names. Not chalked: cut, with pick-points and nails, by people who meant them to outlast them.

CORIN ASHBY, deep and square, with a tally of days beside it that runs on for years. DAVIN, with a line struck clean through it and, under the line, one word: RAN. WILLA, small and low on the wall, where a child could reach. And HESK MARLOW, with the sun of the Dawn scratched round it, the way the valley marks its dead.

Above them all, in letters as tall as a hand: THORNHAVEN."
reexamine_text = "Corin, Davin, Willa, Hesk Marlow. Thornhaven, cut into the white stone."

